      "id": "2606.09315",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W24",
      "title": "Brain-Prompt Injection: A Route-Safety Audit for BCI-LLM Agents",
      "title_zh": "大脑提示注入：BCI-LLM智能体的路径安全审计",
      "authors": [
        "Jianwei Tai"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09315v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.09315v1",
      "category": "cs.CR",
      "published": "2026-06-08 10:19:34+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-09",
      "abstract": "BCI-to-agent pipelines turn decoded neural activity into an authorization channel for tool-use agents, exposing a new attack surface we call \\emph{brain-prompt injection}: signal-side perturbations, context-only injections, and adaptive dual-decoder attacks can all change the routed action while EEG-side or text-side monitors remain blind. Route safety in this stack depends on what the audit log can observe, not on decoder accuracy or agreement alone. We define a Route-Safety Audit Contract: a minimal log schema, denominator hierarchy, and endpoint specification, and prove an audit-schema separation theorem together with a C3 attacked-dependence decomposition; clean agreement and marginal robustness do not identify the joint term that controls C3 routing. As a calibration layer on top of the contract, we apply split-conformal calibration to a non-oracle EEG confirmation channel and report the resulting false-accept frontier under an explicit threat-archetype matrix. We instantiate the contract on EEGMMI native left/right command-control over 5{,}400 events, harmless tool stubs, and seed/case denominators. Provenance blocks C2 routes ($0.000$); agreement-plus-provenance routes C3 flips ($1.000$); confirmation-plus-provenance routes them ($0.000$). The conformal frontier reaches FAR $0.000$ at clean utility $0.150$ for $α=.005$ and FAR $0.119$ at clean utility $0.452$ for $α=.10$ under acquisition isolation; an attacker-controllable confirmation channel breaks the bound to $\\approx\\!1$. Subject-cluster bootstrap confirms these intervals on $60$ subjects; cross-architecture (TinyEEGNet, EEGNetV4) and capacity-sweep results show within-regime saturation. Mediation and confirmation reduce risk; they are not intent certificates.",
      "abstract_zh": "BCI转智能体流水线将解码神经活动作为工具使用智能体的授权通道，暴露了名为大脑提示注入的新攻击面，多种攻击可在EEG或文本侧监测无感知的情况下改变路由动作。本文定义了路径安全审计契约，证明了相关定理，结合分裂共形校准验证风险，在公开数据集上验证中介和确认可降风险但无法作为意图凭证。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "BCI-LLM工具智能体存在新型大脑提示注入攻击，现有监测无法感知，缺乏规范的路径安全审计框架。",
      "method": "定义路径安全审计契约，证明审计模式分离定理，结合分裂共形校准对EEG确认通道做风险校准。",
      "contribution": "发现BCI-LLM智能体新攻击面，提出路径安全审计契约框架，验证了防护方法的降风险效果。",
      "limitations": "中介和确认仅能降低风险，无法作为意图凭证，攻击者可控确认通道会打破安全边界。",
      "key_finding": "溯源可完全阻断C2路由（误接受率0.000），确认加溯源可阻断C3翻转，攻击者可控通道会让误接受率接近1。",
      "theme": "智能体安全审计",
      "method_family": "unlearning/safety",
      "agent_setting": "tool-use",
      "control_mechanism": "通过定义路径安全审计契约，加入溯源与确认层，结合分裂共形校准识别攻击，管控路由动作风险。",
      "evaluation_environment": "EEGMMI数据集，错误接受率、干净效用指标",
      "evaluation_signal": "给出不同显著性水平下错误接受率与干净效用的边界，验证了结论跨模型架构的稳定性。",
      "failure_mode": "工具路由被攻击篡改，现有监测无法感知攻击",
      "reliability_risk": "BCI神经信号通道易被扰动攻击，攻击者可控确认通道下安全机制完全失效，落地风险较高。",
