      "id": "2606.12908",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W24",
      "title": "SENTINEL: Failure-Driven Reinforcement Learning for Training Tool-Using Language Model Agents",
      "title_zh": "SENTINEL：面向工具使用语言模型智能体的失败驱动强化学习",
      "authors": [
        "Ziyi Wang",
        "Yuxuan Lu",
        "Yimeng Zhang",
        "Qun Liu",
        "Chen Luo",
        "Jiri Gesi",
        "Hanqing Lu",
        "Yisi Sang",
        "Manling Li",
        "Jing Huang",
        "Dakuo Wang"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.12908v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.12908v1",
      "category": "cs.CL",
      "published": "2026-06-11 05:06:50+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-12",
      "abstract": "Language model agents are increasingly effective in solving realistic tasks through multi-turn tool use. However, training reliable tool-using agents remains challenging in practice. While reinforcement learning provides an on-policy paradigm for improving agents from their own environment interactions, its effectiveness depends heavily on the training task distribution. When tasks are fixed before training, the task distribution can become increasingly mismatched with the policy's evolving capabilities, causing many rollouts to be spent on uninformative tasks. We propose SENTINEL, a failure-driven reinforcement learning framework that turns the Solver's rollout failures into targeted training tasks. SENTINEL follows a Controller--Proposer--Solver loop: the Controller analyzes failed trajectories and summarizes recurring error patterns, the Proposer generates executable tasks that stress these weaknesses, and the Solver is trained on the targeted tasks. On Tau2-Bench Retail with Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507, SENTINEL improves Pass\\^{}1 from 66.4 to 74.9 and outperforms RL on general synthetic tasks across Pass\\^{}k metrics. These results demonstrate that model failures provide an effective and scalable source of targeted training signal for improving tool-using language model agents.",
      "abstract_zh": "语言模型智能体可通过多轮工具使用解决现实任务，但训练可靠的工具使用智能体仍存在挑战。强化学习效果高度依赖训练任务分布，固定预训练任务分布会与进化后的策略能力不匹配，大量采样浪费在无信息任务上。本文提出SENTINEL失败驱动强化学习框架，遵循控制器-提议器-求解器循环，将失败转化为针对性训练任务，在Tau2-Bench Retail任务上提升了性能，效果优于通用合成任务的强化学习方法。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "训练工具使用语言模型智能体时，固定预训练任务分布与进化后策略能力不匹配，大量采样浪费在无信息任务上。",
      "method": "提出SENTINEL失败驱动强化学习框架，采用控制器-提议器-求解器循环，将失败轨迹转化为针对性训练任务。",
      "contribution": "验证框架可有效提升工具使用智能体性能，证明模型失败是可扩展的有效针对性训练信号源。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "在Tau2-Bench Retail上，SENTINEL将Qwen3-4B智能体的Pass@1从66.4提升到74.9，性能优于常规强化学习。",
      "theme": "工具使用智能体训练",
      "method_family": "tool-use control",
      "agent_setting": "tool-use",
      "control_mechanism": "分析智能体失败轨迹得到错误模式，生成针对性训练任务，以失败驱动的强化学习优化工具使用智能体。",
      "evaluation_environment": "Tau2-Bench Retail，评测指标为Pass@1、Pass@k",
      "evaluation_signal": "在Tau2-Bench Retail零售任务上，SENTINEL将Qwen3-4B智能体Pass@1从66.4提升至74.9，优于普通强化学习方法。",
      "failure_mode": "固定训练任务分布与策略能力不匹配，导致训练采样低效",
      "reliability_risk": "仅在单个基准验证效果，未验证多任务、大模型场景下的泛化性与稳定性。",
      "industrial_relevance": "high",
