      "id": "2606.24820",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W26",
      "title": "SHERLOC: Structured Diagnostic Localization for Code Repair Agents",
      "title_zh": "SHERLOC：代码修复智能体的结构化诊断定位",
      "authors": [
        "Hovhannes Tamoyan",
        "Sean Narenthiran",
        "Erik Arakelyan",
        "Mira Mezini",
        "Boris Ginsburg"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.24820v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.24820v1",
      "category": "cs.CL",
      "published": "2026-06-23 17:05:50+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-24",
      "abstract": "LLM agents solve repository-level coding tasks through multi-turn tool use, but utilize half their budget on locating faults before editing. Dedicated localization frameworks have emerged, yet are still evaluated as file retrieval rather than actionable diagnosis, producing locations without the diagnostic context a repair agent needs. We introduce SHERLOC (Structured Hypothesis-driven Exploration and Reasoning for Localization), a training-free framework pairing a reasoning LLM with compact repository tools and self-recovery, without fine-tuning or multi-agent orchestration. SHERLOC reaches state-of-the-art localization across model scales: 84.33% accuracy@1 on SWE-Bench Lite and 81.27% recall@1 on SWE-Bench Verified; at ~30B parameters, it matches or outperforms other agentic methods. Injecting our locations and diagnostic findings into repair agents yields, on average, +5.95 pp resolve rate on SWE-Bench Verified while cutting localization and total tokens by 36.7% and 23.1%.",
      "abstract_zh": "大语言模型智能体通过多轮工具使用解决仓库级编码任务，但一半预算消耗在故障定位上。现有定位框架仅评估文件检索，无法提供修复所需诊断上下文。本文提出无训练框架SHERLOC，结合推理大模型、轻量仓库工具与自恢复机制，无需微调或多智能体编排，在SWE-Bench系列基准取得定位SOTA，注入修复智能体后可提升解决率并大幅降低token消耗。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "现有代码修复智能体故障定位开销大，现有定位框架仅做文件检索，缺乏修复所需诊断上下文。",
      "method": "提出无训练的结构化假设驱动定位框架SHERLOC，结合推理大模型、轻量仓库工具与自恢复机制。",
      "contribution": "在多个规模模型上取得定位SOTA，注入修复智能体后提升解决率，大幅降低定位与总token开销。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "约30B参数的SHERLOC即可超越其他智能体方法，为修复Agent提升5.95个百分点解决率，减少36.7%定位token。",
      "theme": "代码Agent缺陷定位",
      "method_family": "agent harness",
      "agent_setting": "coding/tool-use",
      "control_mechanism": "提出无需微调的结构化假设驱动推理框架，结合轻量工具与自恢复，优化定位流程降低开销。",
      "evaluation_environment": "SWE-Bench Lite、SWE-Bench Verified，指标含准确率、召回率、解决率、token消耗",
      "evaluation_signal": "在SWE-Bench Verified上，修复Agent解决率提升5.95个百分点，定位token减少36.7%，总token减少23.1%。",
      "failure_mode": "故障定位开销过高，缺乏有效诊断上下文拉低代码修复Agent整体效率",
      "reliability_risk": "仅在公开代码基准测试验证，未测试真实工业级大型代码仓库的落地表现",
