      "id": "2606.26474",
      "direction_id": "agent-skills-harness",
      "direction_name": "Agent Skills 与 Harness",
      "week": "2026-W26",
      "title": "Localizing RL-Induced Tool Use to a Single Crosscoder Feature",
      "title_zh": "将强化学习诱导的工具使用定位于单个交叉编码器特征",
      "authors": [
        "Andrii Shportko",
        "Shubham Bhokare",
        "Ahmed Zeyad A Alzahrani",
        "Bowen Cheng",
        "Gustavo Mercier",
        "Jessica Hullman"
      ],
      "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2606.26474v1",
      "pdf_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.26474v1",
      "category": "cs.LG",
      "published": "2026-06-25 00:17:11+00:00",
      "collected": "2026-06-26",
      "abstract": "Fine-tuning through RL reshapes the internal representations of language models to enable agentic behaviors such as tool use, yet the mechanistic basis of these changes remains poorly understood. While RL substantially improves structured tool-call generation, it is unclear which features emerge, which are preserved, and whether identified features can be leveraged for retraining-free behavioral control. In this work, we show that $\\textit{Dedicated Feature Crosscoders (DFC)}$ isolate a compact set of RL-specific features that mediate tool-calling capability in $\\texttt{Qwen2.5-3B}$. Across a $48$-crosscoder hyperparameter sweep, encode-decode reconstruction improves the RL model's tool correctness by $+31.1 \\pm {9.7}$ pp and passively transfers tool-calling ability to the frozen base model by $+6.8 \\pm 5.0$ pp which we call a $\\textit{capability spillover}$. Our findings show that DFC partitioning concentrates RL-introduced capability into a minimal, steerable feature set that enables runtime behavioral control of agentic LLMs.",
      "abstract_zh": "强化学习微调会重塑大语言模型内部表征以实现工具使用等智能体行为，但这类变化的机制基础仍不清晰，也不清楚涌现出哪些特征、能否用已识别特征实现无重训练行为控制。本文提出专用特征交叉编码器（DFC），分离出介导Qwen2.5-3B工具调用能力的RL特异性紧致特征集，可将RL模型工具正确率提升31.1±9.7个百分点，还能向冻结基座模型溢出+6.8±5.0个百分点的工具调用能力，实现智能体大模型运行时行为控制。",
      "has_code": false,
      "repo_url": "",
      "repo_stars": 0,
      "hf_upvotes": 0,
      "citation_count": 0,
      "venue": "",
      "venue_year": "",
      "venue_type": "",
      "venue_url": "",
      "venue_confidence": "",
      "venue_source": "",
      "is_authority_venue": false,
      "ingest_source": "",
      "manual_reason": "",
      "manual_tags": [],
      "problem": "强化学习微调让大模型获得工具调用能力，但该能力的机制基础不清晰，也未明确特征能否用于无重训练行为控制。",
      "method": "提出专用特征交叉编码器DFC，分离出介导工具调用能力的紧致RL特异性特征集，实现运行时行为控制。",
      "contribution": "验证了DFC可将RL引入的能力浓缩到极小可引导特征集，可提升工具正确率并向冻结基座溢出能力。",
      "limitations": "摘要未提及",
      "key_finding": "DFC可提升RL模型工具正确率31.1±9.7个百分点，能向冻结基座溢出+6.8±5.0个百分点的工具调用能力。",
      "theme": "工具调用控制",
      "method_family": "tool-use control",
      "agent_setting": "tool-use",
      "control_mechanism": "定位强化学习诱导的工具调用相关交叉编码器特征，分离出紧致特征集，通过特征调控实现运行时行为控制。",
      "evaluation_environment": "摘要未提及",
      "evaluation_signal": "以工具调用正确率为核心指标，验证了DFC对RL模型和冻结基座模型的工具能力提升效果。",
      "failure_mode": "摘要未提及",
      "reliability_risk": "未在真实落地任务场景验证效果，仅做模型内部特征分析，方法的实际通用性尚不明确。",
